A||||11||ChadMan||"Iron Duke Cup" -- racing series idea||||10||
Z||000000||ChadMan||02-15-2001||10:52 AM||||It'll never happen, of course.  But imagine how much fun it would be to watch (and/or participate in) the "Iron Duke Cup" racing series!<P>Rules:<P>1)  All races take place on oval tracks no bigger than 1/2 mile.  Total length of races not to exceed 50 miles.<BR>2)  Series is open to any 1984-1986 Pontiac Fiero with 2.5 4-cyl engine.  (No 87-88 Dukes due to 6 hp advantage.)  Engines must use stock intake/TBI, ignition componentry, and stock exhaust manifold.  Engine rebuilding is permitted but must use stock block, head, and cam profile.  Roller lifters are permitted; roller rockers are forbidden.  No mufflers/cats required.<BR>3)  Transmission must be 4-sp Muncie or 5-sp Isuzu.  Any clutch is permitted.<BR>4)  All cars must use stock 14" alloy wheels with 215/60R14 street tires.  Tread shaving is permitted but not required.<BR>5)  All cars must use stock 84-86 rotors and calipers.<BR>6)  All cars must retain stock ride height.  Koni-type adjustable shocks are prohibited.<BR>7)  Roll cage required.  Removal of interior trim and passenger seat is permitted.  All external body panels must be retained.<BR>8)  To keep costs down, all cars are subject to $4000 claim -- that is, any competitor may purchase any other competitor's car for $4000.<P>Like I say, it'll never happen.  But wouldn't it be fun as hell?<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||02-15-2001||11:40 AM||||Hey Chad, you can't leave us 87-88 guys out...add a weight penalty or something to make up for the 6 horse advantage. And the 88 guys must also have an additional penalty for the 88 suspension improvments. (I'd smoke Ya...teheehee)||||reg||6
Z||000002||Black88GT||02-15-2001||11:42 AM||||Make sure the track as ample amount of firefighters....<P><BR>hehe||||reg||11
Z||000003||JohnnyK||02-15-2001||01:34 PM||||50 miles.. Yeah, and spectators who don't mind being there for a few days..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Roll cage though? Your dreaming dude.. I don't know if my 4 banger is any slower than any one elses, but at that speed, I'll take my chances with the pavement.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||02-15-2001||01:35 PM||||As we've seen at Mid-Ohio, Dale, right now you would DEFINITELY smoke me.  Maybe the new EGR valve I'm putting in next weekend will help?<P>Firefighters?  We don' need no steeking firefighters!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>On a half-mile oval, any self-respecting Duke ought to be able to reach 70 mph or so.  (How big's the oval at Indianapolis Raceway Park?)  If I hit a stationary object at 70 mph, I want a roll cage.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||02-15-2001||01:49 PM||||There was a topic about something relating to this on the Fiero Racing list a year or so ago.  It was about Spec fiero racing.  Seemed like a good idea but it just kinda faded away.  That would be cool to race beater 2m4s.  Little bumping here and there.  Going to the junkyard to get extra panels would be easy.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||02-15-2001||01:53 PM||||I'm in!<P>But ah, I guess I'd have to swap all my GT facias and panels back.  Could you possibly change that rule?  Aerodynamics don't really play that much of a role at the speeds we'd be going at anyway.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Still have my 14" alloy wheels, that's ok.<P>Could you drop the rollcage part?  Interior is too nice to cut up.  Like JohnnyK said, I'll take my chances.<P>Black88GT, we'll probably have drivers from other heats marshall the track.  If everyone brings a fire extinguisher along, we should be ok.<P>oh ya, I'd want car #01, called it first!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dukeboy.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||14
